{{see also|norse}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Partly from {{bor|en|nl|Noorsch}} (now {{m|nl|Noors|t=Norwegian}}), from {{m|nl|noordsch|t=northern; nordic}}; and partly from {{bor|en|da|norsk|t=Norwegian}}. Both equivalent to {{af|en|north|-ish|nocat=1}}. {{doublet|en|Norsk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|nôrs}}, {{IPA|en|/noɹs/|[no̞ɹs]}}
*: {{audio|en|en-us-Norse.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/nɔːs/}}
*: {{audio|en|en-uk-Norse.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)s|s=1}}
* {{a|horse-hoarse}}<!--{{q|without the ''horse-hoarse'' merger}}-->
** {{a|rhotic}} {{IPA|en|/nɔːɹs/}}
** {{a|nonrhotic}} {{IPA|en|/nɔːs/}}

